# .dockerignore — files that must NOT be copied into the Docker image
#
# Security rationale:
# - .env may contain secrets (API keys, paths, tokens); NEVER ship it in an image.
# - .git/ exposes full commit history, contributor names, and repo metadata.
# - *.pt weight files can be hundreds of MB and must be mounted at runtime, not baked in.
# - logs/ and runs/ are runtime artefacts that should not be part of the build context.
# - __pycache__ / *.pyc files are environment-specific byte-code and add no value.

# Secrets and configuration
.env

# Version control metadata
.git/
.github/

# Model weights (large files; mount via -v at runtime instead)
weights/
*.pt

# Runtime artefacts
logs/
runs/
datasets/

# Demo video files (large; mount via -v at runtime)
demo/*.mp4
demo/*.avi
demo/*.mov
demo/*.mkv
demo/*.webm

# Python byte-code
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
